STRICT 9-FRAME 16:9 GRID LAYOUT (3x3):
Frame 1: Extreme Wide Shot (subject tiny in large environment);
Frame 2: Low-Angle Wide Shot (ground level, focusing on full body silhouette);
Frame 3: Classic Medium Shot (Waist-up, looking at camera);
Frame 4: Extreme High-Angle (looking vertically down at top of head);
Frame 5: Profile Shot (Side view, elongated features);
Frame 6: Dutch Angle (horizon tilted 30 degrees, cinematic tension);
Frame 7: Over-the-shoulder shot (looking at a detail in environment);
Frame 8: Three-quarter Medium-Close Up;
Frame 9: Macro ECU (tightest detail on skin texture or eye). MANDATORY: No text on image. No captions, no labels, no watermarks, no overlays. Pure cinematic imagery only.

